    "text": "How to apply:\n  1. Choose how to apply: online, on paper at the Maple Ridge Leisure Centre, or through a third party\n  2. Fill in the Financial application form\n  3. Upload or hand in your documents, or have a third party complete the adjudicator section\n  4. Wait for an email or phone call about your application\n  5. Pick up your membership card at the Maple Ridge Leisure Centre or Albion Community Centre\n  6. Re-apply each year\nWhat you need:\n  - An address-related bill from the last 3 months. PO Box addresses are not accepted\n  - A Notice of Assessment for each person contributing to household income, or government assistance documents such as GIS, SAFER, EI or income assistance\n  - Not needed if a third party verifies you: proof of address and income\nPractical tips:\n  - Not discounted, among others: private swimming lessons, high performance training camps, contracted or partner programs over [amount — see the guide], licensed afterschool care and employment certification.\n  - Rename your uploaded files with your last name.\n  - A third party can be a social worker, caseworker, counsellor, school principal, community agency or medical provider.\n  - Online registration applies your discount automatically. Email Registration@MapleRidge.ca for your first sign-in link.\n  - Applications needing extra screening can take up to 14 days.\nHow long it takes (verified — you may state this): Up to 10 business days",
